cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this counterexample using the metadata below and identify the commit or release consulted."
title: "A Counterexample to Restricted Bell Real-Rootedness"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ozols
    given-names: Chris
    website: "https://github.com/cozuya"
url: "https://github.com/cozuya/restricted-bell-counterexample"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cozuya/restricted-bell-counterexample"
abstract: >-
  The restricted Bell polynomial B_(800,<=5), counting finite labeled set
  partitions with block sizes at most five, has a nonreal complex root.
  This refutes the real-rootedness assertion of Conjecture 6.4 of Moll,
  Ramirez, and Villamizar (2017). The unconditional Lean 4.28.0 proof with
  Mathlib v4.28.0 uses only propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound,
  including kernel-checked integer arithmetic and the combinatorial
  coefficient bridge. Original and independent Python verifiers are
  included. No minimality, classification, or novelty claim is made.
keywords:
  - restricted Bell polynomials
  - restricted Stirling numbers
  - real-rootedness
  - set partitions
  - counterexample
  - Hankel matrix
  - formal proof
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
